      "segmentId": "m00040:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00040:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "The ball and stick models and bond-line structures of cyclopropane, cyclobutane, cyclopentane, and cyclohexane, positioned from left to right."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_04_01_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00002",
      "segmentId": "m00040:para:para-00002"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00040:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00040:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "The chemical structures of methylcyclopentane and 1-cyclopropylbutane. In 1-cyclopropylbutane, 3 carbons form a ring and 4 carbons form a straight chain."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_04_01_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00005",
      "segmentId": "m00040:para:para-00005"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00040:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "The correct and incorrect numbering of substituted cyclohexane. The name with correct numbering is 1,3-dimethylcyclohexane and with incorrect numbering is 1,5-dimethylcyclohexane because 1,3 is a lower locant than 1,5. 3 and 5 are labeled lower and higher, respectively."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_04_01_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00004",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00040:alt:fig-00004-alt",
          "text": "One correct and two incorrect numberings of a substituted cycloheptane. The name with the correct numbering is 2-ethyl-1,4-dimethylcycloheptane. The names with incorrect numberings are 1-ethyl-2,6-dimethylcycloheptane and 3-ethyl-1,4-dimethylcycloheptane."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_04_01_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00007",
      "segmentId": "m00040:para:para-00007"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00005",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00040:alt:fig-00005-alt",
          "text": "The correct and incorrect numbering of a substituted cyclopentane. The name with correct numbering is 1-ethyl-2-methylcyclopentane and the name with incorrect numbering is 2-ethyl-1-methylcyclopentane."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_04_01_005.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00008",
      "segmentId": "m00040:para:para-00008"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00006",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00040:alt:fig-00006-alt",
          "text": "The correct and incorrect numbering of a substituted cyclobutane. The name with correct numbering is 1-bromo-2-methylcyclobutane and the name with incorrect numbering is 2-bromo-1-methylcyclobutane."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_04_01_006.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00009",
      "segmentId": "m00040:para:para-00009"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00007",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00040:alt:fig-00007-alt",
          "text": "The chemical structures of 1-bromo-3-ethyl-5-methyl-cyclohexane, (1-methylpropyl)cyclobutane or sec-butylcyclobutane, and 1-chloro-3-ethyl-2-methyl-cyclopentane, positioned from left to right."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_04_01_007.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
